  "asylum": {
   "title": "On the Record",
   "outcome": "success",
   "text": [
    "Captain's log, stardate 4432.1. Forty-one Ilvari refugees and one stubborn freighter captain are now formally under Concord protection. The Tellarch Compact has lodged a protest. Admiral Thorne has forwarded the camp records to the Concord Council with a three-word cover note: \"Read this. Today.\"",
    "Captain Reyes has asked whether the Meridian is hiring. I told her we would talk."
   ]
  },
  "favor": {
   "title": "Varr Hospitality",
   "outcome": "success",
   "text": [
    "Captain's log, stardate 4432.1. The Patience of Stone was, regrettably, seized by Varr raiders before it could be transferred to Compact custody. Sensor logs of the incident were degraded by nebular interference.",
    "Three days later, Ossa Free Port registered forty-one new residents and one freighter. Its steward AI sent us a message. It read, in its entirety: \"THANK YOU. I AM CHEERFUL.\""
   ]
  },
  "accord": {
   "title": "By the Book",
   "outcome": "success",
   "text": [
    "Captain's log, stardate 4432.1. The Patience of Stone and its passengers were transferred to Tellarch Compact custody in accordance with the Kessel Accords. Commander Vael was courteous.",
    "Dr. Okafor has filed a formal dissent in the medical log. I have not asked him to withdraw it."
   ]
  },
  "defiance": {
   "title": "An Incident",
   "outcome": "success",
   "text": [
    "Captain's log, stardate 4432.1. Following an exchange of fire with a Compact patrol cutter, the refugees are aboard the Meridian. The Compact calls it an act of aggression. Without documentation, Concord Command cannot easily call it anything else.",
    "I made the right choice. I made it the hard way."
   ]
  },
